
Request A (Category Audit): "Get a list of all content titles that belong to the 'Documentaries' 
category, was released in 2024 and has a rating higher than 8.0. We need the Title and the 
Category Name in the final report." 



SELECT 
    c.title AS "Content Title",
    cat.category_name AS "Category"
FROM content c
INNER JOIN category cat ON c.category_id = cat.category_id
WHERE cat.category_name = 'Documentaries'
  AND c.release_year = 2024
  AND c.rating > 8.0
ORDER BY c.title;





Request B (Success Score Analysis): "We don't just want to know Views or Ratings 
separately. We need a combined 'Success Score' for our dashboard." 
● Write a query that returns the Title and a new column named success_score. 
○ success_score = rating + views_in_millions 
● Only show results where this calculated success_score is greater than 100.


SELECT 
    c.title AS "Content Title",
    cat.category_name AS "Category",
    c.rating AS "Rating",
    c.views_in_millions AS "Views (millions)",
    (c.rating + c.views_in_millions) AS "Success Score"
FROM content c
INNER JOIN category cat ON c.category_id = cat.category_id
WHERE (c.rating + c.views_in_millions) > 100
ORDER BY "Success Score" DESC;
